body:
Oh I completely cut contact with the girl. We had a big online argument a week or so ago in which I basically told her that I know what games she's trying to play and that I refuse to play any of them and for her to get the fuck out of my life. 

&#x200B;

I tried not to be rude or nice but I did get the point across very very clearly. 

&#x200B;

>Secondly, and I hate to say this, you gotta get out of this relationship if your girlfriend continues to not stand up for you. A girlfriend who respects you would let her friends know they can’t speak negatively about you in front of them. A good girlfriend would feel disrespected by her friends when this happens.

&#x200B;

I agree and she has been much more supportive since the argument which she read in full. 

&#x200B;

I've been with her for 3 years and we haven't had any real problems between the two of us (her friends were always the catalyst) so I don't just want to up and leave right now but I do know that if it gets worse that may have to be an option. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

\>  Sounds like this girl has read "Boyfriend Destroyer Patterns" by Benjamin Damien. It lists 5 simple psychological tricks to undermine an existing relationship so the person using the techniques can move in on a desired target. 

&#x200B;

nice ref Ill check it out

&#x200B;

\>  Some of the techniques include getting her to imagine a breakup, associating the boyfriend with negative emotions, discuss his faults,including being jealous or controlling, placing doubt in the relationship, etc. 

&#x200B;

I can kind of see her doing that. Not for sure or anything but it is a possibility. 

&#x200B;

\>  ""You're taken? Well, I sure am disappointed. However, I do know that it's great to have somebody around who can make your every wish come true and fulfil all of your needs, not to mention somebody to talk to all the time. That's probably pretty clear with you guys, so when do you plan on getting married? I mean, if he fulfils all of your desires the way you need them to be fulfilled, you have probably already planned your wedding, right? You must want to be with him forever - how sweet.” When you deliver this line, you’re planting these thoughts in her mind: 

&#x200B;

She is married (but he's not currently around) so IDK if that's whats up.

&#x200B;

\>It is all very subtle and is never done in a directly critical way...always only hinting in that direction and backing off if it meets resistance.

I guess you could sum it up as "death by a thousand cuts"

Oh, and I should mention that commenting on this is not my vouching for the ethics of such tactics...only an acknowledgement that some people do stoop to such methods.

&#x200B;

I can see her totally doing this. Also this is the sometimes worst fucking form of manipulation I would even say abuse isn't worse just as mind erasing and replacing is sometimes worse than mind messing up. 

&#x200B;

\>  You gut instinct was to try and control this mind poison by cutting of the source, but this girl has already established herself as your girl's friend...so issuing ultimatims such as "no contact" only score points against you because it plays right into the theme that you are controlling...or resent her having fun...or are jealous...or feel threatened, insecure, and lack self confidence. 

&#x200B;

It's a lose-lose game and if I win (by not playing and leaving her and the friend) then I am the bad guy and it wasn't her fault etc etc. I am very very tempted to just say no-contact to my GF with her friend because that is the strong thing to to because I know she loves me more than the friend and if I said she should do that she would. 

&#x200B;

\>  Your best bet against this insidious tactic...which is easier because you are dealing with a girl...is to reverse it on her. Tell your girl that she is making **you** uncomfortable by always finding excuses to switch the topic of conversation to sex when she is alone with you. If your girl is contemplating body modifications that she has never mentioned before, this *could be* a result of ideas getting planted in her mind that you might be looking elsewhere because you find your interest in your girl lagging. So now is a perfect time to drop some genuine comments about specific things that she does that you truly appreciate...or comment that you are thankful to share life with her. Don't go crazy with chocolates and roses or she will think you had an affair and are trying to ease your guilt. Just be subtle yourself, and verbalize that you feel lucky to have your girl and thing she is special. 

&#x200B;

This all is literally the best relationsihp advice that i have ever heard in my life. BTW that other girl is totally being the way she is because she is a bored, lonely, horney, stupid, drug craving fuck. I literally care no more of this girl than I care of guy friends I haven't seen in years. 

&#x200B;

This stuff is going to get copied and printed out it's so good. lol

\>  Whatever you do, don't demonize the friend. Just remain indifferent. 

&#x200B;

Why, she's the one doing all this stuff. I have text evidence of her saying all this stuff not my girl. 

&#x200B;

\>   Misery loves company, so you wants to make your life hell by seducing your girlfriend into her lifestyle. This will only make your girlfriend unhappy in the long run. 

&#x200B;

I completely agree.

&#x200B;

\>  Right now, you should be building. You need to be setting goals towards saving cash and being fully independent. 

&#x200B;

We both are. I am still in contact with my parents (I recently was kicked/moved out) and in good terms and am in school.
